        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. Continuous employment: Each full and complete year of continuous employment is defined for purposes of this entire Article as continuous employment without absence of more than thirty (30) regular working days during the employee's anniversary year, excluding only paid Holidays, paid Sick Leave, paid Vacations, Annual Military Training, authorized Jury Service, paid Bereavement Leave, Temporary Layoff, and Industrial Injury Leaves of one hundred eighty (180) calendar days or less. Continuous employment is computed from an employee's anniversary date of employment which is defined as the date an employee initially commences work, less the periods of adjustment provided in other Sections of this Article VII. A full and complete year of continuous employment begins on the employee's anniversary date as adjusted according to this Article VII and ends at the completion of the shift immediately preceding the next anniversary date",
